==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|en|cold|sore}}, probably for the tendency of the vesicles to recur along with other illness, or possibly during cold weather, though this explanation is less common.<ref>{{R:OED Online|cold sore|n|345783|December, 2012}}</ref> Compare synonym {{m|en|fever blister}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkoʊld ˌsɔɹ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[bump]] (namely a [[vesicle]]) on the lips resulting from [[infection]] by [[herpes simplex]] viruses (mostly [[HHV1]] but also [[HHV2]]).

====Synonyms====
* {{q|colloquially}} {{l|en|fever blister}}, [[herpes]]
* {{q|scientifically}} [[herpes labialis]], [[herpes simplex]], [[herpes simplex 1]]

